From: QVAC SDK Pod <noreply@tether.io>
Subject: [PATCH] chatterbox: NULL-check buffer_w after ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors in load_s3gen_gguf

ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors() can legitimately return NULL when the
underlying backend allocation fails (Metal heap exhaustion, jetsam-induced
memory pressure on iOS warm relaunches, etc.).

In src/chatterbox_tts.cpp, load_s3gen_gguf() does not check buffer_w and
proceeds straight into a per-tensor ggml_backend_tensor_set() loop. With
buffer_w == NULL, every tensor's tensor->buffer is NULL, and tensor_set
hits a GGML_ASSERT inside the backend interface, calling ggml_abort()
and raising SIGABRT.

This is asymmetric with all 8 other ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors call
sites in tts-cpp (s3tokenizer.cpp:384, s3tokenizer.cpp:598,
voice_encoder.cpp:266, t3_mtl.cpp:1564/1652/1704, supertonic_gguf.cpp:334,
chatterbox_engine.cpp:361), which all NULL-check and
fprintf-log-or-throw on failure.

Reproduces on iPhone 16 (iOS 26.4.2) running tests-qvac TTS suite
(chatterbox) with --skip-build after a prior run held the app at
~3 GB peak (jetsam-eligible). Faulting frame is the s3gen preload
thread spawned in tts_cpp::chatterbox::Engine::Impl::Impl().

Fix: throw std::runtime_error symmetrically with the other call sites
so the chatterbox engine constructor surfaces a clean
"alloc s3gen weights buffer failed" error instead of aborting the
process. This pairs with the prior NULL-guard fix in ggml-speech's
ggml_backend_metal_buffer_type_alloc_buffer (which converts the same
failure mode from a hard SIGSEGV into a NULL return).

---
 tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_tts.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_tts.cpp b/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_tts.cpp
--- a/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_tts.cpp
+++ b/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_tts.cpp
@@ -292,6 +292,11 @@ static model_ctx load_s3gen_gguf(const std::string & path, int n_gpu_layers, boo
         m.tensors[name] = dst;
     }
     m.buffer_w = ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors(m.ctx_w, m.backend);
+    if (!m.buffer_w) {
+        gguf_free(g);
+        ggml_free(tmp_ctx);
+        throw std::runtime_error("load_s3gen_gguf: ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors failed for s3gen weights buffer (backend out of memory?)");
+    }
     for (ggml_tensor * cur = ggml_get_first_tensor(m.ctx_w); cur; cur = ggml_get_next_tensor(m.ctx_w, cur)) {
         ggml_tensor * src = ggml_get_tensor(tmp_ctx, ggml_get_name(cur));
         ggml_backend_tensor_set(cur, ggml_get_data(src), 0, ggml_nbytes(src));
